<title>AUSTRALIA: RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT FRANCE 29-15.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT FRANCE 29-15.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat France 29-15 (halftime 6-8) in the first rugby union test at the Sydney Football Stadium on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Tries: Mitch Hardy (2). Conversions: John Eales (2). Penalties: Eales (5)</p>
<p>France - Tries: Philippe Bernat-Salles, Thomas Castaignede. Conversion: Richard Dourthe. Penalty: Dourthe</p>
